7. Core Logic as Executable Pseudocode
7.1 Create Medical Claim
function createMedicalClaim(claim, files, provenance, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "depositor"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Validate the claim against the schema. If invalid, return an error with the details.

Step 3. If the work reference is present, look it up. If null, flag it as unresolved.

Step 4. If the full-pipeline result reference is present, look it up. If null, flag it as unresolved.

Step 5. If the null-model result reference is present, look it up. If null, flag it as unresolved.

Step 6. If the verification result reference is present, look it up. If null, flag it as unresolved.

Step 7. If the replication tracker reference is present, look it up. If null, flag it as unresolved.

Step 8. Generate a claim ID. Set the fields: version 1, moderation_status pending, deposit_date now, depositor_id from auth, depositor_affiliation from auth, provenance from provenance.

Step 9. Insert the medical claim.

Step 10. Insert the outcome records, the evidence records, the adverse events, the serious adverse events, the safety signals, the conflicts, the funding sources, the revisions, and the claim relations.

Step 11. Insert the links if present.

Step 12. Insert the provenance.

Step 13. Insert the moderation record.

Step 14. Insert the audit log entry.

Step 15. Return the claim_id and the status created.

7.2 Read Medical Claim
function readMedicalClaim(claimId, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "reader"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Read the claim. If null, return an error.

Step 3. Read the outcomes, the evidence, the safety profile, the conflicts, the funding, the revisions, the relations, the links, the provenance, and the moderation.

Step 4. Reconstruct the deposit.

Step 5. Insert the audit log entry.

Step 6. Return the deposit.

7.3 Update Medical Claim
function updateMedicalClaim(claimId, claim, provenance, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "depositor"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Read the existing claim. If null, return an error.

Step 3. Validate the new claim.

Step 4. Increment the version. Update the supersedes and superseded_by fields.

Step 5. Insert a provenance record with operation update.

Step 6. Insert an audit log entry.

Step 7. Return the claim_id, the version, and the status updated.

7.4 Delete Medical Claim
function deleteMedicalClaim(claimId, provenance, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "admin"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Read the existing claim. If null, return an error.

Step 3. If soft delete, mark as deleted. Otherwise, remove.

Step 4. Insert an audit log entry.

Step 5. Return the claim_id and the status deleted.

